3,1,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
4,1,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Toshio,,We should ensure our choice is based on evidence. I am interested in whether previous projects actually met the needs of the users.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I agree. We often overlook the operational impact. I want to know how room availability is affected during construction and after completion.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,George,,It is important to consider the people maintaining these facilities. We must see if the current workload is sustainable for the staff.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,We need to be realistic about timelines. I've noticed a pattern of scheduling slips and unforeseen costs that we must account for this time.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A charmingly optimistic approach, but perhaps we should verify if our budget projections actually survive contact with the real market.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, that is a fair point. However, the qualitative experience of the users is just as vital as the quantitative room data.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"True, but without knowing the timetable absorption, we risk creating a bottleneck that disrupts the entire academic year.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,George,,I believe we are ignoring the human element. The physical infrastructure is only as good as the staff who keep it running.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I agree, but if the project timeline collapses, the staff will be under even more pressure. We need to analyze delivery patterns.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. It would be a tragedy to approve a plan based on a fantasy figure that doubles the moment the first brick is laid.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"Then we are in agreement. We need a mix of user satisfaction, operational capacity, and financial history to make a rational decision.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Victoria,,I will focus on the actual usage and the gaps in service. It is the only way to avoid repeating past mistakes.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,George,,I will look into the staffing situation. We cannot keep adding new facilities without adding the hands to manage them.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Mizuki,,I will investigate the site diaries and delivery schedules. I want to see exactly where the delays are happening.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall examine the tender records and the renewal reserves. Let us see how far the ""approved"" costs stray from reality.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
